## Group: Debind
# **A pair, of which exactly one line is ever alive.** A development build carries a second
# SavedVariables file holding the seed flag (`DevSeed.lua`); a release carries only the one. The
# packager deletes the debug block outright and strips the leading "# " off what is in the other,
# so a release ends up with the plain line and a development checkout, where the packager never
# runs, keeps that one commented out and uses the debug line instead.
#
# The space in "# ##" is the whole of that mechanism. Without it the strip leaves the line still
# commented, and a release ships with no SavedVariables line at all. A development checkout cannot
# show that, because there the line is a comment either way.
#
# **Nothing else goes inside either block.** Every line in the non-debug one loses its leading
# "# " in a release, so a comment parked in there comes out as a TOC line every user gets.
#@non-debug@
# ## SavedVariables: DebindVars
#@end-non-debug@
#@debug@
## SavedVariables: DebindVars, DebindDevVars
#@end-debug@
## OptionalDeps: Clique, Grid2, DevTool, ViragDevTool
## AddonCompartmentFunc: Debind_CompartmentFunc
## AddonCompartmentFuncOnEnter: Debind_CompartmentOnEnter
## AddonCompartmentFuncOnLeave: Debind_CompartmentOnLeave
## Notes: Set a keybind once for every character, then override it on one class, one specialization, or one character.|n|nSlash Command: |cffffff00/deb|r
