libs.xml
locales.xml

#@debug@
# The packager deletes this block, contents and all, from a released build. What it holds is one
# generated line naming the checkout the game is loading, which the window title and the login
# message show in place of a version -- a working copy has no version to show. The file is
# gitignored; `npm run stamp:install` puts in the hook that writes it. Without the hook there is
# no file, and `GetVersionLabel` in `Misc.lua` answers "dev".
#
# **Do not write this block's own opening or closing marker inside a comment here.** The filter is
# a line range, so a comment quoting the closing marker ends the range early and the file name
# below survives into the TOC every user gets. That is not hypothetical -- it happened once.
DevStamp.lua
#@end-debug@

Debind.xml

#@debug@
# The written development profile and the command that plants it, for a client that has none or
# one this build cannot read. **Two things keep it out of a release, and both are needed**: the
# packager deletes this block, and `.pkgmeta`'s ignore list keeps the file out of the staging copy.
# Unlike `DevStamp.lua` above, this one is committed source, so with only the TOC line removed the
# file itself would still be copied into the addon folder.
#
# **Do not write this block's own opening or closing marker inside a comment here**, for the reason
# spelled out on the block above.
#
# After `Debind.xml` because it reads `Constants` when it loads.
DevSeed.lua
#@end-debug@

DebindUI.xml

# The two panels of the sharing tabs. **After `DebindUI.xml`, because they are declared as children
# of `DebindFrame`** (`parent=` + `parentKey=`), and a parent named before it exists is a frame with
# no parent. They came over from `DebindStorage` with the addon boundary: the UI is Debind's and what
# stays over there is the strings and the drawer (`devdocs/building-export-import.md`).
ExportUI.xml
ImportUI.xml

# The Switches tab, a child of `DebindFrame` for the same reason and with the same requirement:
# after `DebindUI.xml`. It is not a sharing panel and reads nothing from the load-on-demand addon -
# what it draws is the switch definitions, which are ordinary profile data.
SwitchesUI.xml

# Also after `DebindUI.xml`, but for the other reason: it wears `DebindDialogTemplate`, and a
# template named before it is declared is an inherit that finds nothing. It is not a child of
# `DebindFrame` - it stands over whatever asked for a key.
KeyCapture.xml

SpellPicker.xml

Public.lua